\title{smalldta: Write Compact Stata '.dta' Files}
\description{
Writes data frames to Stata '.dta' files using, for every variable, the smallest storage type that holds its values exactly. This applies the same demotions as Stata's 'compress' command (double to long, int or byte; str# sized to the longest value; strL only when needed) at write time, so files are as small as Stata itself would make them and need no post-processing. Supports formats 117, 118 and 119 (Stata 13 through Stata 19), value labels, variable labels, dates and extended missing values, with no dependencies beyond base R.
